{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SytEntryMono","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SytEntryMono","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sq_content_gap_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sq_content_gap_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytEntryMono.lean#L251-L264","doc":"**`d² ≠ 1`** for consecutive labels in different rows and columns.  Together with\n`content_ne_of_succ` (`d ≠ 0`), this is the full admissibility of an `AdjacentSwapStep`\nbetween the two cells: `|d| ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sameCol_of_content_pred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sameCol_of_content_pred","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytEntryMono.lean#L198-L249","doc":"**Content gap `−1` ⇒ same column** (for consecutive labels).  The column-transpose of\n`sameRow_of_content_succ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sameRow_of_content_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sameRow_of_content_succ","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytEntryMono.lean#L157-L196","doc":"**Content gap `+1` ⇒ same row** (for consecutive labels).  If `q` carries the successor label\nof `p` and `content q = content p + 1`, then `p` and `q` are in the same row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.entryLtCol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.entryLtCol","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytEntryMono.lean#L145-L155","doc":"Entries strictly increase down a column (general row gap). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.entryLtRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.entryLtRow","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytEntryMono.lean#L133-L143","doc":"Entries strictly increase along a row (general column gap). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.content_ne_of_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.content_ne_of_succ","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytEntryMono.lean#L63-L131","doc":"**Consecutive labels never share a diagonal.** If cell `q` carries the label one greater\nthan cell `p` (`entry q = entry p + 1`), then `p` and `q` have different content\n`(col − row)`.  A shared content would place a cell carrying a label strictly between the two\nconsecutive labels — impossible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.entryLtOfDiagRowLt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.entryLtOfDiagRowLt","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytEntryMono.lean#L34-L61","doc":"Entries strictly increase along a diagonal: same content, strictly smaller row ⇒ strictly\nsmaller entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.entryLtDiagSucc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.entryLtDiagSucc","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytEntryMono.lean#L27-L32","doc":"Entries strictly increase along the immediate diagonal step `(i,j) → (i+1,j+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}